{"format":1,"manifest":{"name":"laravel-artisan","publisher":"vyloxi","version":"1.0.1","displayName":"Laravel Artisan","description":"Run artisan from the command palette: a guided make: wizard for 27 generators, migrate, queue, cache, scheduler and tinker commands, with Sail support.","engines":{"ferrum":"^0.1.0"},"categories":["Tools"],"icon":"icon.png","repository":"https://github.com/voukengdongmofrankysteve/ferrum-market","license":"MIT","main":"extension.js","activationEvents":["onCommand:laravelArtisan.make","onCommand:laravelArtisan.run","onCommand:laravelArtisan.history","onCommand:laravelArtisan.migrateToStep","onCommand:laravelArtisan.modelShow","onCommand:laravelArtisan.migrate","onCommand:laravelArtisan.migrateStatus","onCommand:laravelArtisan.migrateRollback","onCommand:laravelArtisan.migrateFresh","onCommand:laravelArtisan.seed","onCommand:laravelArtisan.routeList","onCommand:laravelArtisan.optimizeClear","onCommand:laravelArtisan.configClear","onCommand:laravelArtisan.cacheClear","onCommand:laravelArtisan.viewClear","onCommand:laravelArtisan.keyGenerate","onCommand:laravelArtisan.storageLink","onCommand:laravelArtisan.serve","onCommand:laravelArtisan.queueWork","onCommand:laravelArtisan.queueRestart","onCommand:laravelArtisan.queueFailed","onCommand:laravelArtisan.queueRetryAll","onCommand:laravelArtisan.scheduleWork","onCommand:laravelArtisan.scheduleList","onCommand:laravelArtisan.tinker","onCommand:laravelArtisan.about","onCommand:laravelArtisan.eventList","onCommand:laravelArtisan.test"],"permissions":["terminal","workspace.read"],"contributes":{"commands":[{"command":"laravelArtisan.make","title":"Make: New Model, Controller, Migration...","category":"Laravel Artisan"},{"command":"laravelArtisan.run","title":"Run Any Artisan Command...","category":"Laravel Artisan"},{"command":"laravelArtisan.history","title":"Run a Recent Artisan Command Again","category":"Laravel Artisan"},{"command":"laravelArtisan.migrateToStep","title":"Rollback N Migration Steps...","category":"Laravel Artisan"},{"command":"laravelArtisan.modelShow","title":"Show Model Details (model:show)...","category":"Laravel Artisan"},{"command":"laravelArtisan.migrate","title":"Migrate","category":"Laravel Artisan"},{"command":"laravelArtisan.migrateStatus","title":"Migration Status","category":"Laravel Artisan"},{"command":"laravelArtisan.migrateRollback","title":"Rollback the Last Migration Batch","category":"Laravel Artisan"},{"command":"laravelArtisan.migrateFresh","title":"Fresh Migrate and Seed (erases the database)","category":"Laravel Artisan"},{"command":"laravelArtisan.seed","title":"Run Seeders","category":"Laravel Artisan"},{"command":"laravelArtisan.routeList","title":"List Routes","category":"Laravel Artisan"},{"command":"laravelArtisan.optimizeClear","title":"Clear All Caches (optimize:clear)","category":"Laravel Artisan"},{"command":"laravelArtisan.configClear","title":"Clear Config Cache","category":"Laravel Artisan"},{"command":"laravelArtisan.cacheClear","title":"Clear Application Cache","category":"Laravel Artisan"},{"command":"laravelArtisan.viewClear","title":"Clear Compiled Views","category":"Laravel Artisan"},{"command":"laravelArtisan.keyGenerate","title":"Generate Application Key","category":"Laravel Artisan"},{"command":"laravelArtisan.storageLink","title":"Link Storage","category":"Laravel Artisan"},{"command":"laravelArtisan.serve","title":"Serve the Application","category":"Laravel Artisan"},{"command":"laravelArtisan.queueWork","title":"Start a Queue Worker","category":"Laravel Artisan"},{"command":"laravelArtisan.queueRestart","title":"Restart Queue Workers","category":"Laravel Artisan"},{"command":"laravelArtisan.queueFailed","title":"List Failed Jobs","category":"Laravel Artisan"},{"command":"laravelArtisan.queueRetryAll","title":"Retry All Failed Jobs","category":"Laravel Artisan"},{"command":"laravelArtisan.scheduleWork","title":"Run the Scheduler Locally","category":"Laravel Artisan"},{"command":"laravelArtisan.scheduleList","title":"List Scheduled Tasks","category":"Laravel Artisan"},{"command":"laravelArtisan.tinker","title":"Open Tinker","category":"Laravel Artisan"},{"command":"laravelArtisan.about","title":"About This Application","category":"Laravel Artisan"},{"command":"laravelArtisan.eventList","title":"List Events and Listeners","category":"Laravel Artisan"},{"command":"laravelArtisan.test","title":"Run Tests (artisan test)","category":"Laravel Artisan"}],"keybindings":[{"command":"laravelArtisan.make","key":"Ctrl+Alt+M"}],"configuration":{"title":"Laravel Artisan","properties":{"laravelArtisan.runner":{"type":"string","default":"auto","description":"How artisan is started: auto (Sail if vendor/bin/sail exists, else php), php, sail, or docker-compose."}}}}},"files":{"icon.png":{"encoding":"base64","content":""},"extension.js":{"encoding":"utf8","content":"// Laravel Artisan: run artisan from the command palette. A guided make: wizard for every generator, the everyday migrate, cache,\r\n// queue and test commands, and the right runner (php, Laravel Sail or docker compose). Commands are typed into the terminal where you see them.\r\n\r\n/** Arguments are checked, never trusted: a name may only hold letters, digits and a few path characters. */\r\nconst SAFE = /^[A-Za-z0-9_\\\\/.:@=-]+$/;\r\nfunction safeArg(v) {\r\n  const s = String(v).trim();\r\n  if (!s) throw new Error('The name is empty.');\r\n  if (!SAFE.test(s)) throw new Error('\"' + s + '\" has characters that are not allowed here (use letters, digits and _ - . / \\\\ : only).');\r\n  return s;\r\n}\r\n\r\n/** What types the make wizard offers: artisan command, extra flags the person can tick, and a hint for the name. */\r\nconst MAKES = {\r\n  Model: { cmd: 'make:model', hint: 'Post', flags: [['-m', 'migration'], ['-f', 'factory'], ['-s', 'seeder'], ['-c', 'controller'], ['-r', 'resource controller'], ['-p', 'policy'], ['--all', 'everything above plus requests']] },\r\n  Controller: { cmd: 'make:controller', hint: 'PostController', flags: [['--resource', 'resource methods'], ['--api', 'API methods (no create/edit)'], ['--invokable', 'single action'], ['--singleton', 'singleton resource']] },\r\n  Migration: { cmd: 'make:migration', hint: 'create_posts_table', flags: [['--create=', 'create a table (asks the name)'], ['--table=', 'change a table (asks the name)']] },\r\n  'Form request': { cmd: 'make:request', hint: 'StorePostRequest', flags: [] },\r\n  Resource: { cmd: 'make:resource', hint: 'PostResource', flags: [['--collection', 'a collection']] },\r\n  Middleware: { cmd: 'make:middleware', hint: 'EnsureUserIsAdmin', flags: [] },\r\n  Policy: { cmd: 'make:policy', hint: 'PostPolicy', flags: [['--model=', 'for a model (asks the name)']] },\r\n  Seeder: { cmd: 'make:seeder', hint: 'PostSeeder', flags: [] },\r\n  Factory: { cmd: 'make:factory', hint: 'PostFactory', flags: [['--model=', 'for a model (asks the name)']] },\r\n  Event: { cmd: 'make:event', hint: 'OrderShipped', flags: [] },\r\n  Listener: { cmd: 'make:listener', hint: 'SendShipmentNotification', flags: [['--event=', 'for an event (asks the name)'], ['--queued', 'queued']] },\r\n  Job: { cmd: 'make:job', hint: 'ProcessPodcast', flags: [['--sync', 'run synchronously']] },\r\n  Mail: { cmd: 'make:mail', hint: 'OrderShipped', flags: [['--markdown=', 'markdown view (asks the name)']] },\r\n  Notification: { cmd: 'make:notification', hint: 'InvoicePaid', flags: [['--markdown=', 'markdown view (asks the name)']] },\r\n  Command: { cmd: 'make:command', hint: 'SendEmails', flags: [] },\r\n  Rule: { cmd: 'make:rule', hint: 'Uppercase', flags: [] },\r\n  Provider: { cmd: 'make:provider', hint: 'RiakServiceProvider', flags: [] },\r\n  Observer: { cmd: 'make:observer', hint: 'PostObserver', flags: [['--model=', 'for a model (asks the name)']] },\r\n  Cast: { cmd: 'make:cast', hint: 'Json', flags: [] },\r\n  Enum: { cmd: 'make:enum', hint: 'OrderStatus', flags: [['--string', 'string backed'], ['--int', 'int backed']] },\r\n  Scope: { cmd: 'make:scope', hint: 'ActiveScope', flags: [] },\r\n  Test: { cmd: 'make:test', hint: 'PostTest', flags: [['--unit', 'a unit test'], ['--pest', 'a Pest test'], ['--phpunit', 'a PHPUnit test']] },\r\n  'Blade component': { cmd: 'make:component', hint: 'Alert', flags: [['--inline', 'no view file'], ['--view', 'view only']] },\r\n  'Livewire component': { cmd: 'make:livewire', hint: 'posts.create', flags: [['--inline', 'inline view'], ['--test', 'with a test']] },\r\n  Channel: { cmd: 'make:channel', hint: 'OrderChannel', flags: [] },\r\n  Exception: { cmd: 'make:exception', hint: 'PaymentFailed', flags: [['--render', 'with a render method']] },\r\n  View: { cmd: 'make:view', hint: 'posts.index', flags: [['--pest', 'with a Pest test']] },\r\n};\r\n\r\n/** The program that runs artisan. */\r\nfunction runnerPrefix(runner, hasSail) {\r\n  if (runner === 'sail' || (runner === 'auto' && hasSail)) return './vendor/bin/sail artisan';\r\n  if (runner === 'docker-compose') return 'docker compose exec app php artisan';\r\n  return 'php artisan';\r\n}\r\n\r\nfunction build(prefix, command, args = []) {\r\n  return [prefix, ...String(command).trim().split(/\\s+/).map(safeArg), ...args.map(safeArg)].join(' ');\r\n}\r\n\r\n/** The artisan arguments for one make: choice. `values` holds the answers for flags that end with \"=\". */\r\nfunction makeArgs(type, name, flags = [], values = {}) {\r\n  const t = MAKES[type];\r\n  if (!t) throw new Error('Unknown kind: ' + type);\r\n  const args = [safeArg(name)];\r\n  for (const f of flags) {\r\n    args.push(f.endsWith('=') ? f + safeArg(values[f] ?? '') : f);\r\n  }\r\n  return { command: t.cmd, args };\r\n}\r\n\r\nconst TASKS = [\r\n  ['laravelArtisan.migrate', 'Migrate', 'migrate'],\r\n  ['laravelArtisan.migrateStatus', 'Migration Status', 'migrate:status'],\r\n  ['laravelArtisan.migrateRollback', 'Rollback the Last Migration Batch', 'migrate:rollback'],\r\n  ['laravelArtisan.migrateFresh', 'Fresh Migrate and Seed (erases the database)', 'migrate:fresh --seed', true],\r\n  ['laravelArtisan.seed', 'Run Seeders', 'db:seed'],\r\n  ['laravelArtisan.routeList', 'List Routes', 'route:list'],\r\n  ['laravelArtisan.optimizeClear', 'Clear All Caches (optimize:clear)', 'optimize:clear'],\r\n  ['laravelArtisan.configClear', 'Clear Config Cache', 'config:clear'],\r\n  ['laravelArtisan.cacheClear', 'Clear Application Cache', 'cache:clear'],\r\n  ['laravelArtisan.viewClear', 'Clear Compiled Views', 'view:clear'],\r\n  ['laravelArtisan.keyGenerate', 'Generate Application Key', 'key:generate'],\r\n  ['laravelArtisan.storageLink', 'Link Storage', 'storage:link'],\r\n  ['laravelArtisan.serve', 'Serve the Application', 'serve'],\r\n  ['laravelArtisan.queueWork', 'Start a Queue Worker', 'queue:work'],\r\n  ['laravelArtisan.queueRestart', 'Restart Queue Workers', 'queue:restart'],\r\n  ['laravelArtisan.queueFailed', 'List Failed Jobs', 'queue:failed'],\r\n  ['laravelArtisan.queueRetryAll', 'Retry All Failed Jobs', 'queue:retry all'],\r\n  ['laravelArtisan.scheduleWork', 'Run the Scheduler Locally', 'schedule:work'],\r\n  ['laravelArtisan.scheduleList', 'List Scheduled Tasks', 'schedule:list'],\r\n  ['laravelArtisan.tinker', 'Open Tinker', 'tinker'],\r\n  ['laravelArtisan.about', 'About This Application', 'about'],\r\n  ['laravelArtisan.eventList', 'List Events and Listeners', 'event:list'],\r\n  ['laravelArtisan.test', 'Run Tests (artisan test)', 'test'],\r\n];\r\n\r\nexports._test = { safeArg, MAKES, runnerPrefix, build, makeArgs, TASKS };\r\n\r\nexports.activate = function (context) {\r\n  const runner = () => String(ferrum.settings.get('laravelArtisan.runner') || 'auto');\r\n  let hasSail = null;\r\n\r\n  async function prefix() {\r\n    if (hasSail === null) {\r\n      try {\r\n        // Laravel Sail is only used when the project really runs in its containers: the Sail script is there AND a compose file\r\n        // defines the laravel.test service. Many projects have laravel/sail installed but run on the computer with php.\r\n        // (listFiles never looks inside vendor/, so the files are read directly.)\r\n        const root = ferrum.workspace.root;\r\n        hasSail = false;\r\n        if (root) {\r\n          const sep = root.includes('\\\\') ? '\\\\' : '/';\r\n          const read = async (...parts) => {\r\n            try {\r\n              return await ferrum.workspace.readFile(root + sep + parts.join(sep));\r\n            } catch {\r\n              return '';\r\n            }\r\n          };\r\n          const script = await read('vendor', 'bin', 'sail');\r\n          const compose = (await read('compose.yaml')) + (await read('compose.yml')) + (await read('docker-compose.yml')) + (await read('docker-compose.yaml'));\r\n          hasSail = script.length > 0 && compose.includes('laravel.test');\r\n        }\r\n      } catch {\r\n        hasSail = false;\r\n      }\r\n    }\r\n    return runnerPrefix(runner(), hasSail);\r\n  }\r\n\r\n  async function run(command, args = []) {\r\n    try {\r\n      await ferrum.terminal.run(build(await prefix(), command, args));\r\n    } catch (e) {\r\n      ferrum.window.showMessage(e.message, 'error');\r\n    }\r\n  }\r\n\r\n  const history = async () => (await ferrum.storage.get('history', [])) || [];\r\n\r\n  context.subscriptions.push(\r\n    ferrum.commands.register('laravelArtisan.make', async () => {\r\n      const type = await ferrum.window.showQuickPick(Object.keys(MAKES).map((k) => ({ label: k, detail: MAKES[k].cmd })), { placeholder: 'What do you want to create?' });\r\n      if (!type) return;\r\n      const t = MAKES[type.label];\r\n      const name = await ferrum.window.showInputBox({ prompt: type.label + ' name', placeholder: t.hint });\r\n      if (!name) return;\r\n      const picked = [];\r\n      while (true) {\r\n        const remaining = t.flags.filter(([f]) => !picked.includes(f));\r\n        if (!remaining.length) break;\r\n        const items = [{ label: 'Create it now', detail: picked.length ? 'With: ' + picked.join(' ') : 'No extra options' }, ...remaining.map(([f, d]) => ({ label: f, detail: d }))];\r\n        const c = await ferrum.window.showQuickPick(items, { placeholder: picked.length ? 'Another option? (' + picked.join(' ') + ')' : 'Add an option, or create it now' });\r\n        if (!c) return;\r\n        if (c.label === 'Create it now') break;\r\n        picked.push(c.label);\r\n      }\r\n      const values = {};\r\n      for (const f of picked.filter((x) => x.endsWith('='))) {\r\n        const v = await ferrum.window.showInputBox({ prompt: 'Value for ' + f.slice(0, -1) });\r\n        if (!v) return;\r\n        values[f] = v;\r\n      }\r\n      try {\r\n        const m = makeArgs(type.label, name, picked, values);\r\n        await run(m.command, m.args);\r\n      } catch (e) {\r\n        ferrum.window.showMessage(e.message, 'error');\r\n      }\r\n    }),\r\n    ferrum.commands.register('laravelArtisan.run', async () => {\r\n      const past = await history();\r\n      const typed = await ferrum.window.showInputBox({ prompt: 'php artisan', placeholder: 'migrate --pretend' + (past.length ? '   (last: ' + past[0] + ')' : '') });\r\n      if (!typed) return;\r\n      const parts = typed.trim().split(/\\s+/);\r\n      try {\r\n        await run(parts[0], parts.slice(1));\r\n        await ferrum.storage.set('history', [typed, ...past.filter((x) => x !== typed)].slice(0, 20));\r\n      } catch (e) {\r\n        ferrum.window.showMessage(e.message, 'error');\r\n      }\r\n    }),\r\n    ferrum.commands.register('laravelArtisan.history', async () => {\r\n      const past = await history();\r\n      if (!past.length) return ferrum.window.showMessage('No artisan command run from here yet.');\r\n      const pick = await ferrum.window.showQuickPick(past.map((p) => ({ label: p })), { placeholder: 'Run again' });\r\n      if (pick) {\r\n        const parts = pick.label.split(/\\s+/);\r\n        await run(parts[0], parts.slice(1));\r\n      }\r\n    }),\r\n    ...TASKS.map(([id, , command, danger]) =>\r\n      ferrum.commands.register(id, async () => {\r\n        if (danger && !(await ferrum.window.confirm('This erases every table and seeds the database again. Run ' + command + '?', 'Erase and migrate'))) return;\r\n        const parts = command.split(/\\s+/);\r\n        await run(parts[0], parts.slice(1));\r\n      }),\r\n    ),\r\n    ferrum.commands.register('laravelArtisan.migrateToStep', async () => {\r\n      const n = await ferrum.window.showInputBox({ prompt: 'Rollback how many steps?', value: '1' });\r\n      if (!n || !/^\\d{1,3}$/.test(n)) return;\r\n      await run('migrate:rollback', ['--step=' + n]);\r\n    }),\r\n    ferrum.commands.register('laravelArtisan.modelShow', async () => {\r\n      const doc = await ferrum.editor.active();\r\n      let name = doc && doc.selectedText ? doc.selectedText.trim() : '';\r\n      if (!name && doc && /\\.php$/.test(doc.name || '')) name = (doc.name || '').replace(/\\.php$/, '');\r\n      name = (await ferrum.window.showInputBox({ prompt: 'Model name', value: name })) || '';\r\n      if (name) await run('model:show', [name]);\r\n    }),\r\n  );\r\n};\r\n\r\nexports.deactivate = function () {};\r\n"},"README.md":{"encoding":"utf8","content":"# Laravel Artisan\n\nEvery command is typed into the terminal, so you see exactly what runs.\n\n## Make wizard\n\n**Laravel Artisan: Make...** (Ctrl+Alt+M) asks what to create, its name, then offers the options of that generator one by one: for a model `-m -f -s -c -r -p --all`, for a controller `--resource --api --invokable`, for a migration `--create= --table=`, and so on. It covers 27 generators: model, controller, migration, request, resource, middleware, policy, seeder, factory, event, listener, job, mail, notification, command, rule, provider, observer, cast, enum, scope, test, Blade component, Livewire component, channel, exception and view. Names are checked: only letters, digits and `_ - . / \\ :` are allowed, so nothing odd can reach the terminal.\n\n## Everyday commands\n\nmigrate, migrate:status, rollback (and N steps), migrate:fresh --seed (asks first), db:seed, route:list, optimize:clear, config/cache/view clear, key:generate, storage:link, serve, queue:work, queue:restart, queue:failed, queue:retry all, schedule:work, schedule:list, tinker, about, event:list and test. **Run Any Artisan Command...** keeps your last 20 commands.\n\n## Runner\n\nBy default it uses `php artisan`, and `./vendor/bin/sail artisan` when the project has Laravel Sail. Change **Laravel Artisan: Runner** to force `php`, `sail` or `docker-compose`.\n\nPermissions: terminal (to type the command) and workspace.read (to look for Sail).\n"}}}